IMPORT prelude

-- Two type synonyms may share a name when they take different numbers of
-- arguments. `Cargo OF NUMBER` is the one-parameter synonym and the bare
-- `Cargo` is the other, so the second declaration refers to the first, not
-- to itself. These used to be rejected as "Circular dependency detected
-- between type synonyms" in one declaration order and accepted in the other.

DECLARE Cargo IS A Cargo OF NUMBER
DECLARE Cargo a IS A LIST OF a

DECLARE Slot a IS A PAIR OF a, Slot
DECLARE Slot IS A NUMBER

GIVETH A Cargo
cargo MEANS LIST 1, 2

GIVETH A Slot OF STRING
slot MEANS PAIR OF "x", 41

#EVAL cargo
#EVAL slot
